				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "186c8cf2-50ef-ea85-9a28-c7815f3bb16f")
	)
	(text_box "THE 50R TERM, THE JUMPER SHIPS REMOVED.\nFit only if the source drives 50 ohm.  A ZED-F9T is DESTROYED\nby fitting it: its TIMEPULSE pin is 5 mA absolute maximum and\n3.3 V into 50R asks for 66 mA.\nConversely, leaving it out on an 8 Vpp open-circuit source\nfloats the gate input to about +7.4 V, over the 74LVC1GU04's\n6.5 V absolute maximum.  On this channel it should be FITTED."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 148.59 0)
		(size 95.25 21.59)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 220 220 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4 1.4)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3591e476-0e70-6d03-8fad-9a092e95674d")
	)
	(text_box "WHY THE 74LVC2GU04 (rev B)\nTWO unbuffered inverters on one die: half 1\nsquares, half 2 is its replica bias (item\n18).  U = UNBUFFERED, one gain stage: three\ncascaded stages inside a feedback loop\noscillate, one cannot.\nLVC = 5.5 V tolerant inputs on a 3.3 V rail,\nso a 5 V source survives contact, and no\ninput slew-rate limit: it is meant to run in\nits linear region.\nSC-70-6 (DCK): Nexperia's 74AUP2GU04GW fits\nthe same pads (item 8)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 134.62 166.37 0)
		(size 62.23 34.29)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 220 235 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4 1.4)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "36da07e5-c211-1a50-0a80-134f654125bf")
	)
	(text_box "AT THE INPUT\n3.3 V or 5 V pps\nDC coupled, no droop"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 58.42 269.24 0)
		(size 43.18 10.16)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
